# REQ-006: Document Export (Print, PDF Export, Original Format Download)

**Priority:** Must Have
**Effort:** Low (print + PDF export — pre-built); Medium (original format download — net-new)
**Risk:** Low
**Depends On:** REQ-004 (Document Viewer & Navigation), REQ-005 (File Format Support & Conversion)

> ⚠️ **Implementation note:**
> - **Print** and **Export to PDF** are already implemented as reusable EMIS-X components. **Do not re-implement.** Integrate the existing components.
> - **Download in original file format** is a **net-new capability** and must be implemented. This is the only deliverable in this requirement requiring new engineering work. Original files are preserved at ingestion per REQ-005.

---

## User Story

As a practice administrator or clinician,
I need to export documents in multiple formats — print, PDF, and original file type — 
So that I can share, archive, or escalate documents through appropriate channels.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Users can print a document directly from the viewer. *(Pre-built — integrate only)*
- [ ] Users can export/download a document as a PDF. *(Pre-built — integrate only)*
- [ ] Users can download a document in its original source file format (e.g. Word, RTF, TIFF, CDA XML). *(Net-new — must implement)*
- [ ] The original format download is available for all documents where an original file was preserved at ingestion (per REQ-005).
- [ ] Where no original file is available (e.g. document was ingested directly as PDF), the original format download option is absent or clearly disabled — not silently broken.
- [ ] All three export actions are accessible from within the document viewer without navigating away.

