### Component Specifications

> 🚫 All components use `@emisgroup/ui-*` exclusively.

**Original Download Button (net-new):**
- Component: `Button variant="mono" size="small"` — matches Print and PDF sibling buttons
- Default: `ariaLabel={t('export.original.ariaLabel')}` with icon `~icons/ic/outline-file-download` 20px + label `{t('export.original.label')}`
- Loading: `disabled` + spinner icon `~icons/ic/outline-refresh` (animated) + label `{t('export.original.downloading')}`
- Disabled (no original): `disabled aria-disabled="true" title={t('export.original.unavailableTooltip')}` + icon `var(--text-dim)` opacity 0.5
- Tooltip on disabled: `Popover` or native `title` attribute — `{t('export.original.unavailableTooltip')}` = "Original file not available for this document"

**Placement in toolbar:**
- Document Manager injects `⬇ Original` button into the viewer toolbar slot provided by the pre-built viewer component API
- Positioned after `⬇ PDF` button; no additional separator needed

---

### Interaction Patterns

**Click `⬇ Original` (available):**
1. Button enters loading state immediately (optimistic UI)
2. `GET /documents/{documentGuid}/export/original` — timeout 30s
3. On success: browser download triggers from `Content-Disposition: attachment` response; button returns to default
4. On error/timeout: button returns to default; persistent error `Notification`

**Hover/focus `⬇ Original` (disabled):**
- Tooltip appears after 500ms delay: `{t('export.original.unavailableTooltip')}`
- Keyboard: tooltip visible when button has focus (`role="tooltip"` associated via `aria-describedby`)

---

### Accessibility Requirements (WCAG 2.1 AA)

- [x] Perceivable: button label + icon (not icon-only); disabled state has tooltip with explanatory text
- [x] Operable: Tab to button; Enter/Space triggers download (when enabled); disabled state communicates via `aria-disabled="true"` + tooltip
- [x] Understandable: loading state announced via `aria-live` on button label; error announced via `Notification role="alert"`
- [x] Robust: `jest-axe ^9.0.0`; `Button` is `@emisgroup/ui-button`

**Rule B — loading state announced:**
```tsx
<Button
  variant="mono"
  size="small"
  disabled={isDownloading || !hasOriginal}
  aria-disabled={isDownloading || !hasOriginal}
  aria-describedby={!hasOriginal ? 'originalUnavailableTooltip' : undefined}
  ariaLabel={isDownloading ? t('export.original.downloading') : t('export.original.ariaLabel')}
>
  {/* icon + label */}
</Button>
<span id="originalUnavailableTooltip" role="tooltip">{t('export.original.unavailableTooltip')}</span>
```

---

### Visual Design

**Tokens:**
- Button default: `var(--text)` (inherits from `Button variant="mono"`)
- Button disabled icon/label: `var(--text-dim)`
- Loading spinner: `var(--primary)` (animated `~icons/ic/outline-refresh`)
- Success notification: `var(--positive)` (via `Notification variant="success"`)
- Error notification: `var(--negative)` (via `Notification variant="error"`)

**i18n keys (British English):**
```json
{
  "export.original.label": "Original",
  "export.original.ariaLabel": "Download original file",
  "export.original.downloading": "Downloading…",
  "export.original.unavailableTooltip": "Original file not available for this document",
  "export.original.success": "Original file downloaded successfully.",
  "export.original.error": "Download failed. Please try again."
}
```

---

### Error States

**Download failure (5xx / timeout):** `Notification variant="error"` persistent (no auto-dismiss). `{t('export.original.error')}`. Button returns to enabled default.

**No original available:** Button rendered `disabled`; tooltip explains. No error notification — this is an expected state (not an error).

